section('1. Presentation and demo flow',[
('1.1 Seven slides and 10–11 minutes','Delivered','Created exactly seven slides with a 10:30 speaking plan in the presenter notes. The presentation is saved in Spaces and can be exported through its viewer.'),
('1.2 Clear live-demo transition','Delivered','Slide 7 introduces the live walkthrough of one household from intake through review and correction into the registry.'),
('1.3 Slow narrative and role introductions','Delivered','The notes introduce administrator, intake officer, field officer and reviewer before changing screens. They direct the presenter to pause after each outcome and explain the workflow in plain language.'),
('1.4 Reviewer versus officer permissions','Implemented and tested','Reviewer accounts have the Intake Validator role and no intake edit permission. Tests check rejected create/edit requests and the absence of the Create New Submission control on both domain families. The intake officer cannot approve another actor’s task.'),
('1.5 Dropdown explanation','Delivered','The script explains state, LGA and ward selection before interaction, including consistent answers and reduced typing. It does not imply that GPS verifies the selected administrative area.'),
('1.6 No ad hoc customization promises','Delivered','Presenter notes direct questions into managed follow-up rather than promising implementation during the demonstration.'),
('1.7 Remove persona emails','Delivered','The seven slides contain role descriptions rather than email addresses or credentials. Authentication account identifiers are not shown in the deck.'),
('1.8 Legible shared screens','Implemented and checked','Registry cards wrap text and the intrusive automatic insights overlay is now closed by default. Screens were inspected at 1440×1000. The script specifies a readable sharing resolution, normal zoom and pauses; the meeting host still controls actual screen sharing.')])
section('2. Names, labels and branding',[
('2.1 Master Beneficiary Registry','Implemented','Updated shared catalogue/navigation wording, native registry configuration, intake descriptions, relevant templates and published knowledge articles. Modern/Unified/National Social Registry wording was replaced where found in the active scope.'),
('2.2 NSIPA Unified G2P platform name','Implemented','Retained the platform name while identifying the registry as the Master Beneficiary Registry. The new deck avoids national or government-wide registry claims.'),
('2.3 Remove Nigeria G2P interface branding','Implemented and checked','Checked footer/shared navigation on tested screens. Updated Android display name, its visible splash and mobile download instructions to NSIPA. Existing domain names, compatibility download paths, package identity and signing identity were preserved so links and updates continue to work.'),
('2.4 Remove NSR from labels, titles and IDs','Checked','No NSR text was found in the tested native screen text. The active mobile form identifier is nsipa_field_household_demo and the registry generates HH references. Existing identifiers were not arbitrarily rewritten.'),
('2.5 Household Intake Form','Implemented and verified','Published ODK form title Household Intake Form, version 2026111001. Verified the title, version and new name fields through both ODK domain aliases. Android uses the same form version and field names.'),
('2.6 Household capitalization and labels','Implemented and verified','Updated metadata translations for Households, Individuals, Household name, Household head and Record reference. The house-icon heading now displays Households.'),
('2.7 Data-bridge terminology','Implemented in shared guidance','Applied NSIPA and Master Beneficiary Registry terminology to shared service descriptions and help content. The user’s NCPA-to-NSIPA clarification governs the report and presentation.')])
section('3. Portal and registry display',[
('3.1 Card view by default','Implemented and verified','Registry lists open as cards with an explicit list-view toggle. Existing native search, pagination and record links remain in use.'),
('3.2 Newly created records first','Implemented and verified','Changed the native record-list default from approval-time ordering to descending creation time, with a stable tie-breaker. The newly created test household appears first.'),
('3.3 Required household name','Implemented and tested','Added required household and head name fields to native household metadata. Blank household names are rejected. Updated the domain naming hook so an entered name is preserved during intake, ingestion and functional ID allocation.'),
('3.4 ODK mapping and name display','Verified for the controlled import path','Four fresh fictional submissions were stored in ODK, downloaded back, mapped and imported through the existing native intake API. Each passed two distinct reviewers and reached PROCESSED. Saved household/head names, size, coordinates and reported location matched the source on both registry domains. Immutable source receipts retain the ODK instance and SHA-256. Physical-device capture remains a separate gate.'),
('3.5 Roof and water codes','Verified against a published source dictionary','A separate fictional ODK verification form supplies numeric roof/water choices; the current field form was not changed. All six roof and eight water choices map through their published labels to authoritative registry codes. Fresh imports store CORRUGATED_IRON and PIPED, and both domains display Corrugated iron and Piped. Unknown numeric choices and ambiguous labels are rejected. This does not retrospectively resolve undocumented codes from a different historical form.'),
('3.6 More than one record source','Verified and made visible','Existing records include online household registration, prepared synthetic data and reference demonstration data. Cards now show the recorded source and creation date. A mobile source is not claimed for records without that provenance.'),
('3.7 Mobile names and recent submissions','Implemented with device limit','Android saved visits and ODK instance names now identify the household head. Native cards display a Recent marker for records created within 24 hours. Intake list guidance states its update ordering; a physical mobile synchronization run is still pending.')])
section('4. Review, rework and duplicates',[
('4.1 Online intake through approval','Implemented and tested','A fictional household was saved, submitted, returned, corrected, resubmitted, approved and ingested using the existing backend. Root registration rework/permission regression tests also passed.'),
('4.2 Two review levels','Implemented and tested','Created household intake policy version 2 with a first completeness/duplicate-assessment reviewer and a separate final reviewer. New demo identities have limited client roles. Self-approval and repeat approvers are forbidden. Existing policy history is retained.'),
('4.3 Possible duplicates, including NIN','Checked with limits','Native household duplicate jobs completed and produced scored possible-match evidence. Configured individual rules include an exact foundational_id match alongside names and birth date. This is a configured identifier check, not a verified live NIMC service or a newly validated NIN-specific acceptance test.'),
('4.4 Assess and decide','Delivered','The walkthrough tells reviewers to inspect the possible-match evidence rather than treating a score as proof. The existing approval/return decisions remain the mechanism for acting on the assessment.'),
('4.5 Rejection reason, actor and correction','Implemented and tested','AWE now carries the rejection comment into its callback and the registry response. Rejection returns the submission to editable draft state. The same screen displays the reason, decision actor/time and correction instructions. Root registration also persists a review-history record. Earlier feedback is labelled as historical after a later decision.'),
('4.6 Resubmission and repeated requests','Implemented and tested','Resubmission creates a new AWE request rather than reusing the rejected request. Finalization is locked and repeated requests reuse the pending review. Completed ingestion jobs now ignore duplicate delivery rather than marking an already imported record as failed.'),
('4.7 Stray underscore / not-applicable text','Implemented','Native intake detail text renders standalone missing-value markers as Not recorded and NOT_APPLICABLE as Not required for this stage. Metadata terminology was also corrected. Backend enum values remain unchanged.'),
('4.8 Reliability gate','Applied','The verified registry rework path can be used. Physical-device upload and unconfirmed NPC-attestation steps are not presented as verified live flows. Both controlled and scheduled ODK mapping paths are now verified. The demo excludes unrelated incomplete or unapproved features.')])
section('5. Mobile and offline collection',[
('5.1 Android phone/tablet offline flow','Implemented; hardware check pending','Version 0.7 retains encrypted local draft storage and manual, foreground upload. Names, validation, instance labels, form title and the visible NSIPA splash were updated. The APK builds and verifies with the existing signing key. Older saved samples missing names are prompted to add them and review again before upload. No connected device was available for a fresh phone/tablet test.'),
('5.2 Narrated video of about 30 seconds','Delivered as illustration','Created a 30.000-second narrated MP4 explaining offline save, review and deliberate upload. Every scene is labelled Workflow illustration and states that physical-device verification remains pending. It is not a recording of a successful new device synchronization test.'),
('5.3 Mobile GPS accuracy and manual entry','Implemented; hardware check pending','After the user requests location and grants permission, capture waits for a reported accuracy of 50 metres or better. A 30-second timeout gives retry/manual-entry guidance. Cancellation stops location updates. The 50-metre target is a provisional demonstration default, not a confirmed client policy.'),
('5.4 Browser GPS','Implemented and branch-tested','The existing browser form now waits for the same accuracy target after permission. It supports timeout/denied-permission guidance and manual override, and only saves coordinates with form submission. Simulated tests cover low accuracy, accepted accuracy, manual override, timeout and denial. No claim is made that coordinates verify residence.'),
('5.5 NPC attestation','Awaiting client confirmation','The supplied PDF itself leaves the requirement and relationship to NIMC unresolved. No attestation workflow or eligibility requirement was invented. The client must confirm the attestation purpose, issuer, accepted evidence and decision rules before implementation or demonstration.')])
