section('ODK mapping follow-up: verified results',[
('Integration finding and change','Controlled adapter added','The modern import configuration and legacy ODK importer had no configured mapping. Initially added a strict XML mapper and operator-invoked adapter using existing authenticated intake APIs. The automatic synchronization follow-up now schedules that verified mapping through the same APIs. Both reviewers are still required and no direct registry-table writes are used. The verification form is separate from Household Intake Form.'),
('Cross-domain evidence','Four imports passed','Each domain family accepted one current-form submission and one numeric-choice submission through ODK Central. Source XML was read back from Central before mapping. First review used the intake domain; the independent final review used the other domain. All four reached approved/PROCESSED and each was retrieved from both registry domains, giving eight saved-field checks.'),
('Numeric and retry checks','Passed','Six mapper tests cover all 14 published choices, identical master lists on both domains, missing optional values, unknown codes, ambiguous master labels and invalid source inputs. Adapter checks cover reuse without another create call, changed-source rejection and stopping after an uncertain create outcome. Each live import was called a second time and reused its receipt.'),
('Preserved fields and boundaries','Explicit','Verified household name, head name, total size, country, status, coordinates, altitude and reported-location text against saved API data. Numeric fixtures also verify roof and water codes. Children under 18, shelter, livelihood, needs and GPS accuracy remain in the source/receipt; under-18 children are not incorrectly mapped to an under-five bucket. Reported area names are not asserted as verified geographic IDs. The registry retains STAFF_PORTAL intake attribution; ODK provenance is in the receipt.'),
('Display evidence and location-widget correction','Fixed and verified on both domains','Both numeric records show Corrugated iron and Piped. Corrected Location Details bindings from nonexistent gps_latitude/gps_longitude/address_descriptor fields to stored latitude/longitude/address_line_2. Both coordinates retain six decimal places and signed range validation. Replaced the unsupported accuracy input with stored altitude, clearly labelled Altitude (metres); GPS accuracy remains in the ODK receipt. All four imported records now display 9.896527 latitude, 8.858331 longitude, 1,230 metres altitude and reported-location text on both domains: eight authenticated screen checks. Saved API values still match every mapped field. No record data was rewritten. The shared schema backup is location-schema-before.json; the patch is fix_location_widgets.py, with screenshots and location-checks.json in odk-verification.'),
('Operational handover','Evidence retained','Source: client-concerns/odk_household_mapping.py and pbms-react/odk-registry-import.cjs. Evidence: client-concerns/odk-verification/state.json, source XML, published definitions, source hashes, saved API snapshots, housing screenshots and value-checks.json. Reuse the durable receipt for retries; reconcile any uncertain create outcome before retrying. Do not infer numeric meanings from their position without the source dictionary.')])
