section('Automatic ODK synchronization',[
('Enabled scope and schedule','Live','One systemd timer serves both domain families, which share Central project 1 and the registry backend. It polls approximately 60 seconds after the preceding pass completes and starts with the lab host. Household Intake Form and the separate numeric verification form are allowlisted; their published definitions are SHA-256 pinned. No other forms or changed definitions are silently accepted. Android-to-ODK upload remains manual.'),
('Approval protection','Verified','The dedicated client has Intake Officer permission only. It saves and finalizes new intakes into the existing two-reviewer policy, never approves them. For every new test case, the registry contained zero matching records before approval and after the first reviewer; only the second approval allowed ingestion. The service approval endpoint returned HTTP 403. The ODK reader is a project viewer and was denied form creation.'),
('Duplicate prevention','Verified within source-instance scope','A durable SQLite ledger uses shared backend/project/form/instance identity, independent of hostname. A process lock prevents overlapping workers. The create reservation is committed before the API call; the native submission ID is committed before finalization. Replays reuse the same intake. A lost create response is reconciled read-only against the deterministic record ID and matching fields; uncertain outcomes are held instead of blindly retried. Different ODK instances for the same household still require duplicate assessment by reviewers.'),
('Fresh automatic imports','Four passed','Zainab Sule and Chuka Obi were uploaded through odk.nigeriag2p.com; Aminu Garba and Tomi Adeyemi through g2p-odk.wverve.in. Each domain supplied one current-form and one numeric-form case. The scheduled worker picked them up without a manual import call. Final review used the opposite domain. All four reached PROCESSED and their saved fields, location widgets and readable numeric labels were checked through both registry domains.'),
('Replay and failure checks','Passed','Eight repeated deliveries across both ODK aliases returned 409 duplicate responses. Later polling and a timer restart retained exactly one intake and one registry record for each accepted source. Six worker regression tests covered repeated delivery, a lost response without blind retry, recovery of a committed intake, changed-source holds, invalid numeric codes, and avoiding resubmission of an existing review request. A live lock-contention check confirmed a second worker exits without importing.'),
('Held submissions','Visible operational exceptions','Initially, five older-version sources and two deliberately invalid numeric-code tests were held. The five older demos have now been reviewed and imported using explicitly authorized synthetic names; see the legacy-review section. The two invalid numeric tests have now been reviewed and closed as EXCLUDED_TEST, with no intake created; see the invalid-code review section. Changed source XML is held for manual review and never overwrites an accepted record. Returned or rejected reviews are not automatically resubmitted.'),
('Operations and recovery','Documented','Service: nsipa-odk-sync.service; timer: nsipa-odk-sync.timer. Private state and receipts: /opt/openg2p-lab/odk-sync/. Check status.json and the systemd journal; investigate stale completion timestamps, transient failures and held ledger rows. ODK-Synchronization-Operations.txt documents pause/resume, backups and reconciliation. No external alert channel was configured. Stopping the timer preserves existing reviews and records.')])
p('Verification evidence','SubNS')
p('auto-sync-verification/state.json records each before-review, first-review and after-approval check; final-checks.json records final counts and held reasons. Replay responses, permission denials, worker tests, saved API data and screen captures are retained alongside it. Existing backend services and the location-widget fixes were preserved.')

